# Phase 2: PostgreSQL Database Integration

This implementation plan outlines the transition of the music recommendation system's backend from an in-memory Python list to a persistent PostgreSQL database using SQLAlchemy ORM and FastAPI.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **PostgreSQL Installation Required**: You will need a PostgreSQL database instance running.
> Before starting the execution, please decide whether you want to:
> 1. Install and run PostgreSQL locally on your Windows machine.
> 2. Run PostgreSQL using Docker.
> 3. Use a hosted cloud PostgreSQL service (e.g., Supabase, Neon, or Aiven).
>
> We will need your connection details (host, port, database name, username, and password) to set up the `.env` file.

## 1. Architecture

The updated architecture will transition from stateful in-memory storage to a classic three-tier architecture:

```mermaid
graph TD
    Client[React Frontend <br> localhost:5173] -->|HTTP Requests| API[FastAPI Backend <br> localhost:8000]
    
    subgraph FastAPI Backend
        Router[API Endpoints <br> main.py] -->|Dependency Injection| DB_Session[Database Session <br> get_db]
        DB_Session -->|ORM Queries| Models[SQLAlchemy Models <br> models.py]
        Models -->|Validation/Serialization| Schemas[Pydantic Schemas <br> schemas.py]
    end
    
    DB_Session -->|Driver: psycopg2| PostgreSQL[(PostgreSQL Database)]
    Config[.env File] -.->|Environment Config| API
```

### Key Components
* **React Frontend**: Makes HTTP requests to the backend endpoints.
* **FastAPI Backend (main.py)**: Exposes API routes and uses FastAPI's `Depends` to inject database sessions into path operations.
* **Pydantic Schemas (schemas.py)**: Handles request validation (e.g., creating a song) and response serialization (e.g., returning database objects as JSON).
* **SQLAlchemy Models (models.py)**: Maps Python objects to database tables.
* **SQLAlchemy Engine & Session (database.py)**: Manages connection pools and database sessions.
* **PostgreSQL Database**: The relational database management system storing our persistent data.
* **Dotenv (.env)**: Stores secrets and configurations (database URL) securely and out of the source code.

