## 2. Database Schema

For Phase 2, we will introduce a single relational table representing our song library.

### Table: `songs`

| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `id` | `INTEGER` | Primary Key, Auto-Increment (SERIAL) | Unique identifier for each song |
| `title` | `VARCHAR(255)` | NOT NULL | The title of the song |
| `artist` | `VARCHAR(255)` | NOT NULL | The artist who performed the song |
| `genre` | `VARCHAR(100)` | NOT NULL | The genre of the song |
| `created_at` | `TIMESTAMP` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` | The timestamp when the song record was created |

