## 3. API Design

We will transition the current endpoints and expand them to cover full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) capability.

### Endpoints Reference

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Request Body | Response Status & Body |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **GET** | `/songs` | Get all songs | None | `200 OK` <br> List of Song objects |
| **POST** | `/songs` | Create a new song | `{ "title": "string", "artist": "string", "genre": "string" }` | `201 Created` <br> Created Song object (with ID) |
| **GET** | `/songs/{id}` | Get a single song | None | `200 OK` -> Song object <br> `404 Not Found` -> Error detail |
| **PUT** | `/songs/{id}` | Update a song | `{ "title": "string", "artist": "string", "genre": "string" }` | `200 OK` -> Updated Song object <br> `404 Not Found` -> Error detail |
| **DELETE** | `/songs/{id}` | Delete a song | None | `200 OK` -> `{ "message": "Song deleted successfully" }` <br> `404 Not Found` -> Error detail |

